WEBVTT

00:00:06.141 --> 00:00:07.351
(YELPS)

00:00:07.476 --> 00:00:08.477
(SIGHS)

00:00:09.853 --> 00:00:12.064
Sorry, old girl. I'll fix that.

00:00:16.151 --> 00:00:17.152
(SCREAMS)

00:00:18.028 --> 00:00:19.029
(SHRIEKS)

00:00:22.324 --> 00:00:24.076
-Hey.
-Mr. Moon?

00:00:25.619 --> 00:00:29.414
You probably don't remember me,
but I auditioned yesterday and I...

00:00:29.498 --> 00:00:30.582
BUSTER: Hey, listen.

00:00:30.832 --> 00:00:33.210
Do you think, maybe,
you could reach the ledge?

00:00:33.835 --> 00:00:35.003
That ledge?

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.005
Whoa-oh!

00:00:37.089 --> 00:00:38.673
That's a heck of a trunk you've got there!

00:00:38.882 --> 00:00:40.133
Thanks a lot, kid!

00:00:40.217 --> 00:00:42.427
Uh, Mr. Moon?

00:00:43.095 --> 00:00:45.889
My name is Meena, and I baked a cake for you

00:00:45.972 --> 00:00:49.643
and, uh, I was wondering
if you'd, maybe, give me a second chance to...

00:00:49.726 --> 00:00:50.769
BUSTER: Just a moment, please.

00:00:52.813 --> 00:00:54.147
Be right with you.

00:00:56.691 --> 00:00:57.734
Hmm.

00:00:59.194 --> 00:01:00.487
(STRAINS)

00:01:05.325 --> 00:01:06.743
(PLAYING PIANO)

00:01:06.827 --> 00:01:08.203
(ELECTRICITY CRACKLES)

00:01:08.328 --> 00:01:09.746
MIKE: Yay! It's about time.

00:01:09.830 --> 00:01:10.831
(CONTINUES PLAYING PIANO)

00:01:10.956 --> 00:01:11.957
(GROANS) Johnny...

00:01:12.082 --> 00:01:13.708
Yep, mind your head here.

00:01:13.792 --> 00:01:15.544
Hey, can you pull up that scenic cable?

00:01:15.627 --> 00:01:17.379
-You mean this?
-Yes, that's it!

00:01:20.841 --> 00:01:23.176
Great. And the house lights?

00:01:28.223 --> 00:01:29.224
Wow.

00:01:29.307 --> 00:01:31.768
Oh, I know. Beautiful, isn't she?

00:01:33.061 --> 00:01:34.020
You know what, kid?

00:01:34.104 --> 00:01:35.814
How would you like to be a part of this show?

00:01:35.981 --> 00:01:37.858
Really? Wait, oh, my gosh,

00:01:37.941 --> 00:01:39.317
I was just gonna ask about that.

00:01:39.526 --> 00:01:41.736
Great! Because I could really use a stagehand.

00:01:43.155 --> 00:01:45.031
Stagehand? But...

00:01:45.407 --> 00:01:47.701
Don't worry about it.
You're gonna pick it up in no time.

00:01:47.826 --> 00:01:49.578
I'll teach you everything I know. Follow me.

00:01:49.703 --> 00:01:50.787
(DANCE MUSIC PLAYING)

00:01:50.871 --> 00:01:52.664
These are the rehearsal spaces
and dressing rooms

00:01:52.747 --> 00:01:55.083
and up here,
we got workshops and the main office.

00:01:55.167 --> 00:01:56.751
GUNTER: Up in the air! Touch your toes!

00:01:56.835 --> 00:01:59.838
(VOCALIZING)

00:02:05.093 --> 00:02:06.636
(PLAYING ROCK MUSIC)

00:02:09.764 --> 00:02:11.016
Awesome!

00:02:11.099 --> 00:02:12.184
MIKE: Awesome?

00:02:12.309 --> 00:02:14.561
(SCOFFS) Yeah, I think
the word you're after is "awful."

00:02:14.644 --> 00:02:16.855
And that's me restraining myself.

00:02:17.022 --> 00:02:19.566
There's not an ounce of talent
between them. Not an ounce.

00:02:19.649 --> 00:02:20.775
In fact, you know what?

00:02:20.859 --> 00:02:23.111
I think that prize is as good as mine already.

00:02:27.949 --> 00:02:32.204
Yes, indeed. I am about
to come into a very, very large sum of money.

00:02:32.287 --> 00:02:34.456
$100,000 to be precise.

00:02:34.706 --> 00:02:36.124
Well, is that so?

00:02:36.208 --> 00:02:39.127
In that case, sir,
you'll be wanting our platinum card.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:41.213
(GASPS)

00:02:43.298 --> 00:02:44.674
(CAR HONKS)

00:02:44.841 --> 00:02:46.176
(HIP-HOP MUSIC PLAYING)

00:02:59.439 --> 00:03:01.358
Well, well, well... Hello again.

00:03:04.986 --> 00:03:05.987
(CHUCKLES)

00:03:07.697 --> 00:03:09.074
(BOTH LAUGHING)

00:03:09.157 --> 00:03:12.452
Oh, man, these are
like the cheesiest songs of all time.

00:03:12.536 --> 00:03:13.787
I know, right?

00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:16.623
I mean, I was even thinking of
writing my own song instead.

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:20.085
Wait, what? Your own song?

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:21.211
Well, yeah.

00:03:21.294 --> 00:03:22.879
Look, if you wanna win that money,

00:03:23.004 --> 00:03:25.090
just do what the koala says.

00:03:25.173 --> 00:03:27.300
Why? You think I can't write my own song?

00:03:27.384 --> 00:03:29.177
Whoa, whoa! I'm just saying.

00:03:29.261 --> 00:03:31.388
Not everyone can write songs, okay?

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:35.225
I know I make it look easy, babe. But it's not.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:44.859
Oh, here she is! Quiet down, everybody.

00:03:44.943 --> 00:03:46.236
(ALL SHUSHING)

00:03:46.653 --> 00:03:49.364
So, Meena! Are you in the show?

00:03:50.407 --> 00:03:52.784
Uh, well, yeah. Kinda. But...

00:03:52.909 --> 00:03:54.369
(LOUD CHEERING)

00:03:54.452 --> 00:03:55.579
MEENA'S MOTHER: I knew it! I knew it!

00:03:55.662 --> 00:03:57.163
MEENA'S GRANDFATHER: She did it!

00:03:57.247 --> 00:03:59.499
Oh, I'm so proud of you! I could pop!

00:03:59.708 --> 00:04:01.960
That's my birthday wish
coming true right there!

00:04:02.043 --> 00:04:03.086
Way to go, Meena!

00:04:03.211 --> 00:04:04.713
Oh, Meena, we love you!

00:04:04.796 --> 00:04:06.548
Mom! What the heck?

00:04:06.631 --> 00:04:08.174
Wait a minute, wait a minute.
Don't be mad, okay?

00:04:08.258 --> 00:04:11.469
It was your Grandma.
She told the whole street about your audition.

00:04:11.553 --> 00:04:13.263
-Mom, no, wait.
-Shush, baby.

00:04:13.346 --> 00:04:15.765
You need to save that singing voice of yours.

00:04:15.849 --> 00:04:20.520
So, from now on,
just nod or shake your head, okay?

00:04:21.104 --> 00:04:22.355
(CHUCKLES)

00:04:22.439 --> 00:04:23.982
-(ALL CHEERING)
-(SHUTTERS CLICKING)

00:04:27.068 --> 00:04:28.236
(GROANS)

00:04:30.238 --> 00:04:31.323
How was that, Dad?

00:04:31.406 --> 00:04:33.366
You're still too soft on 'em corners, Johnny.

00:04:33.992 --> 00:04:35.201
-You got to attack 'em.
-(MUSIC PLAYING ON STEREO)

00:04:35.285 --> 00:04:36.870
And you're crunchin' the gears.

00:04:36.953 --> 00:04:39.039
I told you, you got to be gentle with the...

00:04:39.122 --> 00:04:42.042
Look, turn that down. Oi!

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:43.877
Listen to your father!

00:04:44.544 --> 00:04:46.338
"Too soft on the corners, Johnny."

00:04:46.588 --> 00:04:47.839
(TIRES SCREECHING)

00:04:48.006 --> 00:04:50.967
"You're not doin' it right, Johnny.
Speed up, Johnny."

00:04:53.678 --> 00:04:54.929
"Do it like I showed you..."

00:04:55.096 --> 00:04:56.556
Whoa!

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:57.682
(BRAKES SQUEAL)

00:04:57.849 --> 00:04:59.059
(PANTING)

00:04:59.184 --> 00:05:00.393
(TURNS STEREO OFF)

00:05:04.147 --> 00:05:05.398
Dad?

00:05:05.482 --> 00:05:07.275
Oh, no, I've run over my dad.

00:05:08.068 --> 00:05:09.235
-(THUDS)
-(SCREAMS)

00:05:09.319 --> 00:05:10.862
Now, that is more like it.

00:05:10.945 --> 00:05:12.280
-(LAUGHS)
-(SIGHS)

00:05:26.044 --> 00:05:30.799
ROSITA: (ON RECORDING) And the three
little pigs lived happily ever after.

00:05:30.882 --> 00:05:32.509
-Good night, my dears.
-(PIGLETS SNORING)

00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:40.934
Norman, are you awake?

00:05:41.142 --> 00:05:42.519
(MOANS)

00:05:42.602 --> 00:05:44.187
How was your day, honey?

00:05:44.521 --> 00:05:47.065
(YAWNS) Same as always.

00:05:47.732 --> 00:05:49.526
-It was?
-Mmm-hmm.

00:05:50.235 --> 00:05:53.822
I don't know how you do it all, honey.

00:05:53.947 --> 00:05:55.073
Good night.

00:05:55.156 --> 00:05:56.157
Good night.

00:05:57.617 --> 00:06:00.286
(BUSTER MIMICS TRUMPETING)

00:06:04.541 --> 00:06:05.875
(HUMMING)

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:16.136
BUSTER: All creatures great and small,

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:19.347
welcome to the Moon Theater!

00:06:19.806 --> 00:06:21.307
(CHEERING)

00:06:29.482 --> 00:06:30.567
MISS CRAWLY: Mr. Moon?

00:06:31.401 --> 00:06:33.361
I have Judith from the bank.

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:35.989
What? Oh, no, no.
Tell her I'll call her back in the morning.

00:06:36.197 --> 00:06:37.699
I can't.

00:06:37.782 --> 00:06:39.033
She's right here.

00:06:39.492 --> 00:06:40.994
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

00:06:42.495 --> 00:06:44.622
Judith! Hello!

00:06:44.998 --> 00:06:47.625
I work for a bank, not a charity.

00:06:47.709 --> 00:06:49.878
And if your accounts
are not settled by the end of the month...

00:06:49.961 --> 00:06:51.004
Okay. Judith...

00:06:51.171 --> 00:06:54.549
I personally guarantee by the end
of this month this show is going to be

00:06:54.716 --> 00:06:56.843
the biggest hit this city has ever seen!

00:06:56.926 --> 00:06:58.928
Mr. Moon,
none of your shows have ever worked.

00:06:59.012 --> 00:07:00.054
None of them!

00:07:00.221 --> 00:07:01.681
You've had your chances.

00:07:01.765 --> 00:07:05.977
Now settle your accounts
or we will repossess this property!

00:07:06.102 --> 00:07:07.812
Okay. Toodle-oo.

00:07:07.896 --> 00:07:09.272
(LAUGHS NERVOUSLY)

00:07:11.107 --> 00:07:13.568
What are you gonna do, Mr. Moon?

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:15.320
Honestly...

00:07:15.403 --> 00:07:18.406
Uh, I have no idea.

